@startuml j9-language-offline
title J9 Switch language, then reopen the app offline
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName "Noto Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam roundCorner 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
skinparam titleFontSize 17
skinparam titleFontColor #0E5C45
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #0E5C45
  LifeLineBorderColor #7FA89A
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #E8F2EE
  ParticipantBorderColor #0E5C45
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #E8F2EE
  ParticipantFontColor #0B3D2E
  ActorBorderColor #0E5C45
  ActorBackgroundColor #E8F2EE
  ActorFontColor #0B3D2E
  GroupBorderColor #0E5C45
  GroupHeaderFontColor #0E5C45
  GroupBackgroundColor #F3F8F6
  DividerBorderColor #0E5C45
  DividerBackgroundColor #E8F2EE
  DividerFontColor #0B3D2E
  BoxBorderColor #0E5C45
}
skinparam database {
  BorderColor #0E5C45
  BackgroundColor #E8F2EE
}
skinparam note {
  BorderColor #B08A2E
  BackgroundColor #FFF8E6
  FontSize 12
}
actor "Shop owner" as Owner
participant "Browser UI\n(index.html)" as UI
participant "app.js" as App
database "localStorage" as LS
participant "Service worker\n(sw.js)" as SW
autonumber
== Switch language ==
Owner -> UI : pick English, हिंदी or తెలుగు in #lang
UI -> App : change handler: lang = value
App -> LS : setItem('hisaab.lang', lang)
App -> UI : applyLabels(): html lang, every data-i18n label and placeholder
App -> App : render()
App -> UI : names as "Ravi Kumar (रवि कुमार)"; dates in hi-IN or te-IN;\nmessages and reminders in the chosen language
opt Hindi or Telugu digits (#native-digits, shown when not English)
  Owner -> UI : tick
  UI -> App : state.nativeDigits = true
  App -> LS : save()
  App -> App : render(): ₹ amounts and dates in Devanagari or Telugu digits
end
opt light or dark (#theme-toggle)
  Owner -> UI : tap
  UI -> App : toggleTheme(): data-theme on the html element
  App -> LS : setItem('hisaab.theme', next)
end
note right of App : voice quick entry listens in hi-IN, te-IN or en-IN (J3)
== First online visit: install and activate ==
App -> SW : register('sw.js') after the load event
SW -> SW : install: skipWaiting(); caches.open('hisaab-v3').addAll(the app shell:\n./, index.html, styles.css, app.js, sample.js, sample-data.json,\nicon.svg, manifest.webmanifest, and since v1.1 profile.css, profile.js,\nshops.css, shops.js)
SW -> SW : activate: delete every cache except 'hisaab-v3'; clients.claim()
== Online visits keep the cache fresh ==
UI -> SW : GET for a same-origin file, the qrcode-generator script\nfrom cdnjs, or Google Fonts
SW -> SW : fetch(request) from the network first
alt network answers ok (or an opaque cross-origin reply)
  SW -> SW : caches.open('hisaab-v3').put(request, copy)
  SW --> UI : fresh response
end
note right of SW : only GET; other origins, such as Tesseract.js\nfrom jsDelivr, are not handled or cached
== Reopen with no signal ==
Owner -> UI : open the app, no network
UI -> SW : GET index.html, styles.css, sample.js, app.js
SW -> SW : fetch fails
SW -> SW : caches.match(request, ignoreSearch), else index.html
SW --> UI : the last cached copy (?today= still works)
UI -> App : init(), as in J1
App -> LS : getItem('hisaab.lang'), getItem('hisaab.v1')
LS --> App : the same language and the same shop
App -> UI : render() in the saved language
opt offline extras
  App -> UI : UPI QR draws from the cached library once it has loaded online;\nthe screenshot reader says it could not read an amount
end
@enduml
